# S12.1 final review: root Git execution contract

Date: 2026-09-30
Scope: Control PR #203, final same-SHA review P1

## Finding

The recovery barrier intentionally made the canonical Git directories
root-only, but subsequent root Git commands could still consume repository
local hooks/configuration or inherited system/global configuration. A
repository-controlled filter, hook or helper could therefore execute with root
authority.

## Correction

All root Git entrypoints now share one isolated command prefix: empty
environment, disabled system/global configuration, prompts, credentials,
hooks, fsmonitor, maintenance and network protocols, with only the local file
protocol permitted. Before root Git is used, local config files must be regular
single-link bounded files whose keys match the narrow repository metadata
allowlist. Any non-sample hook is rejected. Immutable clone creation and its
generated destination repository are covered by the same contract.

Remote acquisition remains a `chatops` operation. Root consumes only the
sealed, identity-verified local bare repositories after the shared repository
parent has been locked against replacement.

## Verification

Tests assert the isolated root command shape and prove that a configured
filter or executable hook is rejected. No credential value, provider session,
identity data or public runtime state is accessed by this source correction.
